config PER_CORE_HEARTBEAT
	tristate "Per-Core Thread Heartbeat Driver"
	depends on ARM64 && SMP
	default m
	help
	  This driver provides per-core scheduling liveness monitoring based on
	  bound kernel threads.

	  Each target CPU runs a bound heartbeat kernel thread that periodically
	  increments its own heartbeat counter. A monitor thread detects
	  soft-deadlocked (or scheduling-starved) cores by checking whether the
	  counters keep advancing.

	  This complements the IPI Monitor driver (ipi_monitor) to cover soft
	  lockups (L1) that IPI-based detection cannot distinguish.

	  Say M to build this as a loadable kernel module.
